from e import *
E(7,'my-brother-s-great-invention','My Brother\'s Great Invention',
 ('Who invented zero?','Two clues: a concept from ancient Indian mathematicians that adds value to numbers and makes modern calculation possible, and an ancient Indian practice, now popular worldwide, for physical and mental well-being. The answers are zero and yoga. In this story by Anita Rau Badami, a fourteen-year-old tells how her younger brother Anand tries to invent things, with funny and surprising results.'),
 [('Before reading',['You guess inventions from clues, discuss what the world would be like without inventions and discoveries, and fill a grid with missing letters to form words that show qualities of an inventor, such as creativity, curiosity, imagination and determination.']),
  ('The burglar alarm',['The story is told by Anita, who is fourteen. Her brother Anand, a year younger, thinks he is a scientist. He loves tinkering with electrical gadgets, tools, dynamos and planks of wood, and his inventions never work as planned.','One day their father roars from the front door because a bag of water has fallen on him. Anita hisses that it is Anand\'s burglar alarm, and he is getting ready to disappear. Their mother finds Papa sopping wet and scowling.','Anand\'s blueprint shows doors, wires and bells. When the door opens, the alarm clangs and a water bag falls on the thief\'s head, and then they can call the police. He says the alarm works only when the door is opened gently, as a thief would do.','Anita is sceptical but keeps quiet and warns him not to involve her. Papa, who always opens the door softly, gets drenched. For a week, Anand does not try anything new.']),
  ('The time machine',['Then the family watches the film Back to the Future, about a time machine, and the peace of the house ends. Anand\'s room turns into a network of wires, springs, levers and bulbs, with a huge control switchboard, and he does not even comb his hair.','After a fortnight, he announces at lunch that the time machine is ready. Papa says firmly no, and Anand protests that it is an invention. Ma sees his crestfallen look and persuades Papa to at least look at it.','The next day Papa and Ma go to Kharagpur for a wedding, for one night. Anita says they can look after themselves and go next door to Sharma Aunty if needed. Ma makes Anand promise not to touch the time machine, which he does half-heartedly, feeling his creation is not respected.']),
  ('The night visitor',['That night Anand falls asleep and Anita stays up reading a murder story. She hears scratching at the front door and then a rattle and a click. Frightened, she wakes Anand, who mutters groggily at first.','The door swings open, and they see Boppa, a rough-looking man with a green scarf who had recently begun sweeping the compounds in their row of houses. He had picked a time when the family was out. He threatens them with his cudgel and bolts the door from outside.','He comes back and asks which is their father\'s room. Anita is about to point upstairs, but Anand quickly says it is the one next to theirs, which is his time-machine room. Anita is angry, but Anand says it will give them time.','Soon there is a crash and a scream, then muffled thumps, an eerie whine and a low humming. Anand gasps that Boppa has started his time machine. They shout for help.','The neighbours, Mr. and Mrs. Sharma and Dr. Mohan, come running and unlock the door. The children explain hurriedly, and the time machine is still humming softly, but Boppa is gone. They search the house and find nothing.']),
  ('The ending',['Mrs. Sharma thinks he must have run out and been missed, but Anand insists he disappeared into the past through the time machine. Mr. Sharma smiles indulgently at his imagination and stays the night to guard them.','Boppa is never seen again. Papa has the time machine dismantled because he thinks it unsafe, and maybe because he has a niggling suspicion that it worked.','Anand is convinced he is a genius and starts a new project, a telephone to contact creatures in outer space.']),
  ('Thinking about the story',['The cause-and-effect pairs are: Anand rigged the alarm to work on a soft opening, so Papa got soaked; Anita avoided blame because Anand faced the consequences; they saw Back to the Future, so Anand built a time machine; Papa said no because he feared it was unsafe.','Anand did not keep his promise completely. He did not use the machine, but it was used by Boppa, though not through his own action. He gave a half-hearted promise and then led Boppa into the time-machine room.','The correct order is: Anita wakes Anand; the door swings open and Boppa stands there; Anand misleads Boppa into the time-machine room; the neighbours unlock the door.','The narrator introduces herself and her brother to put the reader in the picture. The tone is humorous. Anand is imaginative, inventive and stubborn, and Anita is practical and sceptical.']),
  ('Language work',['Words in the text include racket, a loud disturbing noise; sopping, soaking; scowling, having an angry look; tinkering, experimenting; rigged up, assembled temporarily; sceptical, doubtful; stealthily, quietly so as not to be seen; crestfallen, sad and disappointed; brandishing, waving; cudgel, a short thick stick; groggily, sleepily; and indulgently, fondly.','Repeated structures such as as angry as angry could be and as mad as mad can be show strong feeling, and words like clanging, humming and clattering are sound words that make the story vivid.'])],
 [('Write cause and effect: Anand rigged the alarm to work on a soft opening.',[('Find the effect.','Papa opens doors softly.'),('Write the pair.','The alarm went off and Papa was drenched.')]),
  ('Match: sceptical; crestfallen.',[('Read the glossary.','Sceptical means doubtful.'),('Next word.','Crestfallen means sad and disappointed.')])],
 ('Tell the story of Anand\'s inventions and explain the humour.',['The burglar alarm drenched Papa.','After the film, he built a time machine and promised not to use it.','Boppa the thief entered his room and vanished.','Anand says the machine sent him into the past.'],['Anand was a famous scientist.','Boppa was caught by the police.']),
 ['Anand\'s inventions never work as planned, such as his burglar alarm.','He builds a time machine after watching a film.','A thief called Boppa goes into the time-machine room and vanishes.','Anand believes he is a genius, and plans a telephone to contact outer space.','The story is told by Anita in a light, humorous tone.'],
 [('m','What was Anand\'s first invention in the story?','A burglar alarm',[('A time machine','This comes later.'),('A telephone','This is the next project.')],'The burglar alarm with a water bag drenched Papa.'),
  ('m','Why did the alarm fail?','It worked when the door was opened softly',[('The bag was empty','The bag was full of water.'),('Papa broke the bell','Papa simply opened the door.')],'Papa always opens the door softly, so he got soaked.'),
  ('t','Anand and Anita watched Back to the Future before the time machine.',True,'The film is about a time machine and inspired Anand.'),
  ('m','Who is Boppa?','A man who sweeps the compounds',[('A neighbour doctor','The doctor is Dr. Mohan.'),('Anita\'s uncle','He is a thief.')],'Boppa had recently begun sweeping out the compounds.'),
  ('m','Which room did Anand tell the thief was their father\'s?','His own time-machine room',[('The kitchen','The thief was sent to the room next door.'),('The room upstairs','Anita was about to say this.')],'Anand misled him into the time-machine room.'),
  ('m','What happened to Boppa?','He was never seen again',[('He was caught by neighbours','The neighbours found nobody.'),('He apologised','He disappeared.')],'He vanished, and Anand says he went into the past.'),
  ('m','What does crestfallen mean?','Sad and disappointed',[('Very angry','It is about disappointment.'),('Excited','It is the opposite.')],'Anand looked sad because Papa said no.'),
  ('m','What was Anand\'s new project at the end?','A telephone to contact creatures in outer space',[('A flying carpet','This is not mentioned.'),('A robot','This is not mentioned.')],'He starts a new project after the time machine.'),
  ('s','Who is the author of the story?',['anita rau badami','Anita Rau Badami','badami','Badami'],'The story is by Anita Rau Badami.'),
  ('s','Where did the parents go for a wedding?',['kharagpur','Kharagpur'],'They went to Kharagpur, a few hours from Calcutta (now Kolkata).')],
 keep=['sceptical','crestfallen','tinkering'])
